\n16 Maharashta \nRaja Ramdeo \nAnandilal Podar \n(RRAP) Central \nAyurveda Research \nInstitute, Mumbai  \n589.94 569.85 551.24 \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nNagpur  \n \n422.12 \n \n \n499.44 \n \n \n522.64 \n \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nPune  \n325.75 369.38 371.38 \n17 Nagaland \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Centre, \nDimapur  \n58.26 54.57 57.38 \n18 Odisha \nCentral Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nBhubaneswar  \n554.60 593.74 644.14 \n19 Punjab \nCentral Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nPatiala  \n434.45 480.43 491.83 \n20 Rajasthan \nM. S. Regional \nAyurveda Research \nInstitute, Jaipur  \n1,125.78 896.69 523.64 \n21 Sikkim \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nGangtok  \n262.45 328.67 330.74 \n22 Tamil Nadu \nCaptain Srinivasa \nMurthy Central \nAyurveda Research \nInstitute, Chennai  \n266.85 304.19 304.10 \nDr. Achanta \nLakshmipati \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nChennai  \n181.42 184.19 199.71 \n\n23 Telangana \nNational Centre of \nIndian Medical \nHeritage, \nHyderabad  \n330.78 276.83 278.75 \n24 Tripura \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Centre, \nAgartala  \n116.33 186.13 177.98 \n25 Uttar Pradesh \nCentral Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nJhansi  \n \n267.51 \n \n \n334.32 \n \n \n338.00 \n \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nLucknow \n402.09 372.93 383.67 \n26 Uttarakhand \nRegional Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nRanikhet  \n243.29 229.69 232.63 \n27 West Bengal \nCentral Ayurveda \nResearch Institute, \nKolkata  \n847.31 882.97 891.44 \nTotal 28,068.00 27,262.00 31,697.00 \n \n*Stands merged in National Institute of Sowa-Rigpa since 2021-22 \n \n#Advanced Centre for Ayurveda in Mental Health & Neurosciences, Bengaluru has been \nrenamed as  Regional Ayurveda Research Institute for Mineral and Marine Medicinal \nResources and shifted to Goa. \n \n***** \n ",
