� ���������������� �������������������������� ������ �� ������������������ ������ ������������������ ����\n���������������� �������� ������������������������ ������ ������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������� �������� ���������� ���������������������� �������� �������� ������������ ������������ ������������ ������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������ ���������������� ���������������������� ���������������� ������������ �������������� ������������ ������������ ���� ����������������������\n�������������� ������������������ �������������� ������������������ ������������ ���������������� �������������������������� ������������ ������������\n���������������� ������������ ���������������������������� �������������������� ������������������ ������������������ ���� ������������������ ��������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_167": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *167  \nANSWERED ON 19.12.2022 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT OF YOUTH LIVING BELOW POVERTY LINE \n \n*167.   SHRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR:   SHRIMATI GEETA KORA : \n \n Will the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPR ENEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has prepared any scheme s/action plan for skill \ndevelopment of youth living below poverty line to s kill them and prepare them in \naccordance with the demand of the labour market, if  so, the details thereof, scheme-\nwise in the country including Jharkhand; \n \n(b)  the total number of youth in the country livin g below poverty line who are \nunemployed, State-wise including Jharkhand; \n \n(c) whether the Government has conducted any survey  in this regard and if so, \nthe details thereof; \n \n(d) the number of functional institutions providing  training in skill development in \nvarious States, State-wise; and \n \n(e)  the funds allocated to Jharkhand under the sai d scheme? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (e) A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (E) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 167 TO BE ANSWERED ON 19.12.20 22 ASKED BY \nSHRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR AND SHRIMATI GEETA KORA REGARD ING SKILL \nDEVELOPMENT OF YOUTH LIVING BELOW POVERTY LINE  \n \n(a) There is no specific scheme for skill developme nt of youth living below \npoverty line. However, under Skill India Mission, t he Ministry of Skill Development \nand Entrepreneurship (MSDE) is imparting long-term and short-term training aligned \nto requirements of various sectors of the industry.  To encourage outcome based skill \ndevelopment training for all youth including those living below poverty line, the \nMinistry delivers skill-training through a comprehe nsive network of skill development \ncentres under various schemes viz. Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY), \nNational Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS), Ja n Shikshan Sansthan (JSS) \nand Craftsmen Training Scheme (CTS) through Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs) for \nthe youth across the country.  Brief of these schemes is as under: \n \nPradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY):   PMKVY is a demand-\ndriven Scheme for imparting skill development train ing through Short-Term Training \n(STT) and Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) to yo uth across all States/ Union \nTerritories (UTs). \n \nJan Shikshan Sansthan (JSS) Scheme:  The main target of the JSS is to \nimpart vocational skills to the non-literates, neo- literates and the persons having \nrudimentary level of education upto  8 th  standard and school dropouts upto 12th \nstandard in the age group of 15-45 years, with due relaxation in case of “Divyangjan” \nand other deserving cases. Priority is given to Women, SC, ST, OBC and Minorities. \n \nNational Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS):  This Scheme is for \npromoting apprenticeship training and increasing th e engagement of apprentices by \nproviding financial support to industrial establish ments undertaking apprenticeship \nprogramme under the Apprentices Act, 1961. Training  consists of Basic Training and \nOn-the-Job Training / Practical Training at workplace in the industry.  \n  \nCraftsmen Training Scheme (CTS): This scheme is for providing long-term \ntraining through Industrial Training Institutes (IT Is) across the country. The ITIs offer \na range of vocational/skill training courses coveri ng a large number of economic \nsectors with an objective to provide skilled workfo rce to the industry as well as self \nemployment of youth. \n \n(b) & (c) No data regarding youth living below pove rty line who are unemployed \nis maintained in this Ministry. However, as per the  official poverty estimates released \nby the erstwhile Planning Commission (since been re structured as NITI Aayog), \nState/Union Territory-wise number and Percentage of Population Below Poverty Line \nin India 2011-12 (Based on Tendulkar Methodology) is provided in Annexure-I. \n \n(d) The State/ Union Territory-wise number of Skill  Development Centres under \nPMKVY, JSS, NAPS, and ITIs as on 30.09.2022 is at Annexure-II. \n \n(e) The details of funds released for the State of Jharkhand under PMKVY, JSS, \nNAPS till date are as under: \n(Amount in Rs. Crore) \nScheme PMKVY JSS NAPS Total \nFunds released 210.94 9.31 1.74 221.99 \n \n  \n\nAnnexure I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (B) OF THE LO K SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 167 TO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.20 22 REGARDING \n“SKILL DEVELOPMENT OF YOUTH LIVING BELOW POVERTY LINE” \n \nState wise Number and Percentage of Population Belo w Poverty Line in India: 2011-12 (Based on \nTendulkar  Methodology) \n \nStates/UTs \nRural  Urban  Total  \nPercentage \nof Persons \nNo. of Persons \n(lakhs) \nPercentage \nof Persons \nNo. of \nPersons \n(lakhs) \nPercentage of \nPersons \nNo. of \nPersons \n(lakhs) \nAndhra Pradesh 11.0 61.8 5.8 17.0 9.2 78.8 \nArunachal Pradesh  38.9 4.2 20.3 0.7 34.7 4.9 \nAssam 33.9 92.1 20.5 9.2 32.0 101.3 \nBihar 34.1 320.4 31.2 37.8 33.7 358.2 \nChhattisgarh 44.6 88.9 24.8 15.2 39.9 104.1 \nGoa 6.8 0.4 4.1 0.4 5.1 0.8 \nGujarat 21.5 75.4 10.1 26.9 16.6 102.2 \nHaryana 11.6 19.4 10.3 9.4 11.2 28.8 \nHimachal Pradesh 8.5 5.3 4.3 0.3 8.1 5.6 \nJammu & Kashmir  11.5 10.7 7.2 2.5 10.3 13.3 \nJharkhand 40.8 104.1 24.8 20.2 37.0 124.3 \nKarnataka 24.5 92.8 15.3 37.0 20.9 129.8 \nKerala 9.1 15.5 5.0 8.5 7.1 23.9 \nMadhya Pradesh 35.7 191.0 21.0 43.1 31.6 234.1 \nMaharashtra 24.2 150.6 9.1 47.4 17.4 197.9 \nManipur 38.8 7.4 32.6 2.8 36.9 10.2 \nMeghalaya 12.5 3.0 9.3 0.6 11.9 3.6 \nMizoram 35.4 1.9 6.4 0.4 20.4 2.3 \nNagaland 19.9 2.8 16.5 1.0 18.9 3.8 \nOdisha 35.7 126.1 17.3 12.4 32.6 138.5 \nPunjab 7.7 13.4 9.2 9.8 8.3 23.2 \nRajasthan 16.