    "ls|LS17_S10_U_187": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION N0. 187 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \n DIESEL CONSUMPTION IN RAILWAYS \n \n †187.   SHRI DINESH CHANDRA YADAV: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a)  the extent of success achieved in reducing the  consumption of \ndiesel in Railways; \n(b) the year -wise details of diesel  consumption and the amount  \nspent there upon during the last three years; and  \n \n(c) the time by which the railway electrification project is likely to  be \ncompleted? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND ELECTRONICS & \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n (SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a)  to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 187 BY SHRI DINESH CHANDRA YADAV TO BE ANSWERED \nIN LOK SABHA ON 07.12.2022 REGARDING DIESEL CONSUMPTION IN \nRAILWAYS \n \n(a):  The extent of percentage reduction in c onsumption of High Speed \nDiesel (HSD) oil for three years is as under: \nYear HSD Consumption  \n(Kilo liters) \n% reduction in \nconsumption( year to \nyear) \n2018-19 2641142   \n2019-20 2365299 10.44% \n2020-21 1175901 50.29% \n(Source:  Annual statistical statement)  \n \n (b): The year wise details of diesel consumption and amount spent there \nupon (including Freight and other taxes, etc. for three years is as under:  \nYear HSD Consumption  \n(Kilo liters) \nFuel Bill ( in crores of Rs.) \nAnnual Statistical  \nStatement  \n2018-19 2641142  18587.14 \n2019-20 2365299 16377.60 \n2020-21 1175901 11438.70 \n(Source:  Annual statistical statement)  \n(c): The completion of Electrification projects depends upon various \nfactors like clearances from concerned Departments of State \nGovernments/Central Ministries, completion of Transmission Line works by \nState Power Utilities and resolution of law & order  issu es                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \nduring execution, which are beyond the control of Ministry of Railways. \nTherefore, it is not feasible to fix time lines for completion of projects.  \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_188": " \n   \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \n STARRED QUESTION NO. 188 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/12/2022 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF ROADS THROUGH HOT MIX PLANTS UNDER PMGSY \n \n*188.  SHRIMATI SANGEETA AZAD: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the roads in Uttar Pradesh were being built through hot mix plant under Pradhan \nMantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY); \n(b)  whether the technology of P1P2 has been  implemented in its place only in Uttar Pradesh \nwhereas the roads are being built only through hot mix plant in other States; and \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor? \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n   \n \n(a) to (c) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n  \n  \n\n \n \nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 188 \ndue for answer on 20.12.2022 \n  \n(a) to (c)    As per IRC:SP-72-2015 Manual published by Indian Roads Congress, in all cases of \nroads falling  under traffic categories T1 to T5, surface dressing (single coat (P.1)/ double \ncoat(P.2)) should be preferred as bituminous surfacing. However, 20 mm premix carpet can be \nused as an alternative to surface dressing for traffic categories T6 to T9. Accordin gly, under \nPMGSY, surface dressing (single coat/ double coat) is being adopted on all the roads falling \nunder the traffic category upto T5, whereas, technology of Premix Carpeting with Hot Mix Plant \nis being used on the roads falling under traffic category  T6 to T8. Further as per the Vision \nDocuments on New Technology Initiatives & Guidelines -2022, under T6 to T8 categories, \nsurface dressing is being adopted in 50% of sanctioned road length, as surface dressing has many \nadvantages over premix carpeting. Th e above stipulation is applicable in all the States including \nUttar Pradesh. \n***** \n \n  ",
