�����������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������\n��� ������� ����� ����\n�����������������\n��� ������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������\n�\n��������\n�\n�\n�\n� �\n\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_190": " \n \nO.I.H.\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n1\n90\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n2\n0\nTH\n \n \nDECEMBER\n, 2022\n \n \nPROMOTION OF NATURAL\n \nFARMING\n \nUNDER PKVY \n \n \n†\n*\n1\n90\n.\n \nSHRI\nMATI JYOTSNA CHARANDAS MAHANT\n:\n \n \n \n \n \nWill \n \nthe \n \nMinister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n(a)\n \nthe \nsteps taken by the Government to promote natural farming in the country under \nParamparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY)\n;\n \n \n(b)\n \nwhether any training sessions, workshops and conferences have been organised to \npromote and implement the said scheme/yojana\n;\n \n \n \n(c)\n \nif \nso, the details of the training sessions/ workshops/conferences held in the State of \nChhattisgarh during the last three years;\n \nand\n \n \n(d)\n \nthe percentage of small and marginal farmers benefited by the said scheme/yojana in \nthe country including Chhattisgarh\n?\n \n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a) to (d\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nSTATEME\nNT IN RESPECT OF PARTS (a) TO (\nd\n) OF THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. \n190\n \nDUE \nFOR \nANSWER \nON \n2\n0.12\n.2022 REGARDING \n“\nPROMOTION OF \nNATURAL FARMING UNDER PKVY\n”\n.\n \n \n(a)\n:\n \nGovernment has been promoting organic farming in the country since 2015\n-\n16 through \nthe scheme of Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY). PKVY is being implemented in all \nthe States other\n-\nthan North Eastern (NE) States, across the country. \nThe scheme\n \nprovi\nde end \nto end support to farmers engaged in organic farming i.e. from production to processing, \ncertification and marketing and post harvest management support including processing. Under \nPKVY, farmers of various states in the country are provided financia\nl assistance of Rs 50000/ha \nfor 3 years out of which, Rs 31000/ ha / 3 years is provided directly to farmers through DBT for \non\n-\nfarm and off\n-\nfarm organic inputs. \n \n \nUnder PKVY a total 11.85 lakh\n \nha\n \narea has been covered benefitting 16.19 lakh farmers \nwith total expenditure of Rs. 1758.48 crore during the period 2015\n-\n16 to 2022\n-\n23. \nA total \n8\n \nno. \nof brands\n \nnamely \nMade in Mandla\n, \nOrganic Uttarakhand\n, \nTamil Nadu Organic Product (TOP), \nSahi organic, Nasik Organic & Gadchirrolia Organic Farming\n, Jaivik Jharkhand\n, from the land \nof Jharkhand\n, \nAadim brand of Bhoomi Gadi FPO, Bastar Naturals\n, \nFive Rivers\n \nand \nTripureshwari Fresh\n \nof organic products have been d\neveloped \nin various states \nunder the \nscheme.\n \n \nUnder the \nFlagship Programme of Namami Gange “ARTH GANGE” \nProgramme,\n \n1.23 \nlakh ha area have been covered along the Ganga basin by developing 6181 clusters. Under \nPKVY 131 FPOs have been formed in 17 States/UTs \nunder the provisions of 10,000 FPOs \nScheme\n.\n \n \n \nIn the year 2019\n-\n2020 the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmer’s Welfare initiated a \ncomponent of natural farming under PKVY, \nBharatiya Prakritik Krishi Paddhati (BPKP)\n. \nTraining \nand capacity building are \nintegral part of the scheme. Under BPKP, financial assistance of Rs \n12200/ha for 3 years is provided for cluster formation, capacity building and continuous \nhandholding, certification and residue analysis while Rs. 2000/ha for 3 years is provided to \nfarmer\n \nas incentives through DBT. Moreover, farmers can also avail assistance @ Rs. 8800/ha \nfor 3 years from PKVY funds for marketing, value addition and publicity of natural farming \nproducts. So far 4.09 lakh ha area has been sanctioned to eight States under BP\nKP.\n \n \n\n \n \n \nA Digital web portal (\nnaturalfarming.dac.gov.in\n) has been launched for promotion of \nnatural farming to display information about implementation framework, resources, \nimplementation progress, farmer’s registration, blog etc.\n \n \n(b) \n&\n \n(c):\n \nBPKP Scheme \nguidelines provide for manpower for handholding and capacity \nbuilding through Champion Farmers & Clusters Coordinator (CCCF), Senior Level Resource \nPersons (SLRP), Community Resource Person (CRP), Lead Resource Person (LRP), Cluster \nOffice Management & Dat\na Entry Operations and capacity building, exposure visits and \ntrainings of field functionaries are as under:\n \n \n(i) \n7 days on\n-\nfield practical training including exposure visit to LRPs and CRPs:\n \nOne per year 7 days training including exposure visit to \nNatural farmers for LRPs & CRPs \nto \nbe provided by BPKP/ZBNF experts and Champion Natural Farmers.\n \n(ii) \nYearly Capacity building of all Resource Persons (CRP/LRP/Expert Farmers/SLRP \netc.) by external \nresource persons:\n \n \nOne two days annual capacity building training for all resource persons \n \n(iii) \nCapacity Building of Clusters through Expert Natural Farming farmers/or Agriculture \nGraduate/SLRP:\n \n \n20 Cluster farmers training per year in batch of 50 farmer\ns. \n \n(iv)\n \nTraining of the farmers by LRPs and CRPs:\n \n \n5 trainings of one day duration at village level for all the farmers in a batch of 25 farmers. \n \n \nBPKP under PKVY \nis a \nCentrally Sponsored Scheme, being implemented by the State \nGovernments\n.\n \nT\nhe \ndetails of training sessions/ work\n-\nshops/ conferences held\n/organized by the \nstate\n \nand the beneficiary level data \nare\n \nmaintained at the State level only. \n \n \nThough organization of \ntraining and c\nonferences were held up during 2021\n-\n2022 due to \nCovid Pandemic b\nut during 2022\n-\n2023 (till November, 2022) National Center of Organic and \nNatural Farming (NCONF), a sub\n-\nordinate office of Department of Agriculture & Farmer‘s \nWelfare has organized various training, demonstration and awareness programme (online & \noffline)\n \non natural farming\n \nfor 13055 number of beneficiaries. The \ndetails are\n \ngiven below:\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSl.No. \n \nTraining & awareness Programmes \n \n \nNumber of \nProgrammes \nOrganized \n \nNumber of \nBeneficiaries \n1.\n \n \nOnline/Offline awareness campaign on Organic & \nNatural \nFarming under Azadi\n \nka\n \nAmrit\n \nMahotsav \norganized by N/RCONFs. \n \n60\n \n8554\n \n2.\n \n \nOne Day Farmers Training and Demonstration on \nOrganic and Natural Farming for 50 participants  \n \n17\n \n915\n \n3.\n \n \nTwo Days Training on Organic and Natural Farming for \nExtension Officers/Staff (20 participants) \n \n08\n \n200\n \n4.\n \n \nTwo Days Training on PGS for State Govt. Extension \nOfficers/RCs/SPs/LRPs etc\n \n06\n \n122\n \n5.\n \n \nTrainings on Organic and Natural farming organized as \nCo\n-\nOrganizers by NCONF in association with other \nMinistries/Dept./Govt. & Non Govt. Institutes/SAUs etc\n \n03\n \n405\n \n6.\n \n \nOnline/Offline Training  on\n \nPGS for extension \nofficers/LRPs/RCs/SPs etc\n \n04\n \n84\n \n7.\n \n \nOnline/Offline Farmers Training and Field \nDemonstrations on Organic and Natural farming \norganized by \nN/RCONFs\n \n02\n \n100\n \n8.\n \n \nOffline Awareness Program on organic and natural \nfarming for college \nstudents\n \n02\n \n183\n \n9.\n \n \nParticipation\n \nin Exhibitions / Seminars / Webinars / \nTraining / Workshops / Fairs etc. to disseminate organic \nand natural farming practices.  \n \n36\n \n800\n \n10.\n \n \nAwareness on Organic and Natural farming, PGS \nCertification and Marketing by Guest lectures / Radio \ntalks/TV Talks etc\n. \n \n57\n \n-\n \n11.\n \n \nFarmers Contacted through Outreach Activities for \npopularization of organic and Natural farming\n \n-\n \n1692\n \n \nTotal\n \n195\n \n13055\n \n \nIt has been informed by Chhattisgarh Government that \nt\nhe training activities were \nbanned since last two year due to \nCOVID\n-\n19 situation hence webinar on natural farming for \nChhattisgarh farmers were organized through RCOF Jabalpur to promote and implement the \nsaid scheme/yojana.\n \n \n5 \nWebinars on Natural Farming organized \nduring 2022\n-\n2023 \nby RCOF Jabalpur \nare\n \ngiven below:\n-\n \n \n \n\n\n \n \nS. No.\n \nDate\n \nFarmer\n \n1.\n \n23.06.2022\n \n56\n \n2.\n \n01.07.2022\n \n101\n \n3.\n \n07.07.2022\n \n76\n \n4.\n \n14.07.2022\n \n38\n \n5.\n \n22.07.2022\n \n69\n \n \nTotal\n \n340\n \n \n(d):\n \nBPKP under PKVY is a Centrally Sponsored Scheme being implemented by State \nGovernments;\n \nhence \nthe beneficiary level data (details of small and marginal farmers) is \nmaintained at the state level only. However, the area sanctioned in the country under the BP\nKP \nsin\nce 2020 \n-\n \n21\n \nis given \nbelow:\n \n \nSl. No.\n \nStates\n \nArea in Ha\n \n1.\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n100000\n \n2.\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n85000\n \n3.\n \nKerala\n \n84000\n \n4.\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n12000\n \n5\n \nJharkhand\n \n3400\n \n6.\n \nOdisha\n \n24000\n \n7.\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n99000\n \n8.\n \nTamil Nadu\n \n2000\n \n \nTotal\n \n409400\n \n \n*****\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_191": " \n \n������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n���������������������� ���� ��\n����������������������� ����� �\n�\n�������������������� ��������� �\n�\n†���� � �������������������� ���� �\n� �\n� ������������������������������������������������������ �\n�\n���� ������� ������� ��������� ��� �������� ������ ����� ����� ����������� ����� ���\n�������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n���������������������������������\n�\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������� ����������������������������������������� �\n�\n����������������������������������� �\n�\n���� ���� ��������� ���������� ��� ���� ��������� ��� ������� ���� �����\n��������������� �\n�\n������ �\n�������������������� �������������������� �\n��������������������� ���������������� �\n������ ����������������� �\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������� �\n���� �� ����� ���� ���������� ���������� ������������� ��� �������� ����� ��� ����\n������� ������ ����� �������� ������� –�������� � ��� ������� ��� ���� ��������� ���\n����������������������������� �\n����� ������� ���� ����� ������ ���� ������ ������������ ��� ���� ����� ��������� �����\n�������������� �������������������������������������������� �\n����� �",
