    "ls|LS17_S10_U_201": "  \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *201 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nSAMARTH SCHEME \n \n*201. SHRI SANGAM LAL GUPTA:  \n          DR. RAMAPATI RAM TRIPATHI: \n \n \n Will the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंत्री \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) the  details of implementation of Scheme for Capacity Building in Textile Sector (SAMARTH) \nduring the last five years;  \n \n(b) the State -wise details of total beneficiaries of said scheme, including the States of Uttar Pradesh, \nHimachal Pradesh and Rajasthan;  \n \n(c) the details of total cost borne by the Government in implementation of the said scheme;  \n \n(d) whether the Government plans to scale the said scheme in the States of Uttar Pradesh, Himachal \nPradesh and Rajasthan; and  \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof?  \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र मंत्री (श्री पीयूष गोयल) \nMINISTER OF TEXTILES \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (e):-  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\n  \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *201 TO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \n(a): The Ministry is implementing (Samarth)  - Scheme for Capacity Building in Textile Sector \n(SCBTS), with the objective to provide demand driven, placement oriented National Skill Qualification \nFramework (NSQF) compliant skilling programmes to incentivize and supplement the efforts to the \nindustry in creating jobs in the organised textile (excluding spinning & weaving) and related sectors and \nto provide skilling and skill -upgradation in the traditional sectors. Samarth was initiall y approved for \nimplementation from 2017 -18 to 2019 -20 on 20 thDecember 2017. Guideline of the scheme was issued \non 23.04.2018.  Further, the scheme has been extended up to 31.03.2024. Samarth Scheme was \nformulated under the broad skilling framework adopted by M/o Skill Development & Entrepreneurship.  \nThe scheme is implemented and monitored through a robust digital platform linked with Aadhaar \nEnabled Biometric Attendance System (AEBAS). A t otal of 106 Textile Manufacturers, 12 Industry \nAssociations, 15 State/Central government agencies and 4 sectoral organizations have been on -boarded \nunder the scheme with an allocated target of 4.17 lakh beneficiaries. A total of 1,31,161 beneficiaries \nhave been trained, of which 79,999 have been provided placement. \n \n(b): The State wise details of total beneficiaries including the states of Uttar Pradesh, Himachal \nPradesh and Rajasthan under Samarth scheme is given at Annexure. \n \n(c): The details of fund utilized during the operation of Samarth scheme is as under: \n                                                                                                             (Rs. In crore) \nFinancial Year Fund Utilized \n2017-18 100.00* \n2018-19 16.99* \n2019-20 72.06 \n2020-21 90.70 \n2021-22 85.69 \nTotal 365.44# \n      *During 2017 -18 and 2018 -19, the disbursal was only towards committed liabilities of previous     \nIntegrated Skill Development Scheme (ISDS).  \n       # includes Rs.133.64 crore disbursed as liabilities of previous ISDS. \n(d) & (e): Samarth is a Pan India sc heme implemented on demand driven basis to address the \nskilled manpower needs of textile sector. In addition to allocating targets to textile industry and Sectoral \nOrganizations, all State Governments including States of Uttar Pradesh, Himachal Pradesh and  \nRajasthan were requested for proposals for participation under the scheme. The details of Samarth \nProgrammes with details of participation of state agencies and other implementing partners in these \nStates are given below: \n(Data as on 15.12.2022) \nS. \nNo. State \nNo of Implementing Partners No of \ntraining \ncentres \nNo of \nbeneficiaries \ntrained \nState \nAgencies \nOther Implementing \nPartners \n1 Himachal \nPradesh 0 2 4 219 \n2 Rajasthan 0 8 30 4726 \n3 Uttar Pradesh 2 18 245 17985 \n\n  \nAnnexure \n           State-wise details of total beneficiaries under Samarth Scheme \n \nS. No. States No of beneficiaries trained (as on \n15.12.2022) \n1 ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR 25 \n2 ANDHRA PRADESH 3774 \n3 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 57 \n4 ASSAM 3639 \n5 BIHAR 1578 \n6 CHANDIGARH 88 \n7 CHHATTISGARH 1417 \n8 DELHI 2410 \n9 GOA 29 \n10 GUJARAT 5595 \n11 HARYANA 7424 \n12 HIMACHAL PRADESH 219 \n13 JAMMU AND KASHMIR 1651 \n14 JHARKHAND 1258 \n15 KARNATAKA 25309 \n16 KERALA 1374 \n17 MADHYA PRADESH 2868 \n18 MAHARASHTRA 5912 \n19 MANIPUR 1082 \n20 MEGHALAYA 110 \n21 MIZORAM 425 \n22 NAGALAND 798 \n23 ODISHA 3021 \n24 PUDUCHERRY 255 \n25 PUNJAB 636 \n  \n\n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n**** \n \n \nS. No. States No of beneficiaries trained (as on \n15.12.2022) \n26 RAJASTHAN 4726 \n27 SIKKIM 66 \n28 TAMILNADU 28821 \n29 TELANGANA 4556 \n30 THE DADRA AND NAGAR \nHAVELI AND DAMAN AND DIU \n1200 \n31 TRIPURA 872 \n32 UTTAR PRADESH 17985 \n33 UTTARAKHAND 465 \n34 WEST BENGAL 1273 ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_202": "  \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *202 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nSCHEME TO PROMOTE JUTE INDUSTRY \n \n*202. SHRI ARJUN SINGH: \n \n \n Will the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंत्री \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether the Government is formulating any scheme to promote jute industry in the country;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र मंत्री (श्री पीयूष गोयल) \nMINISTER OF TEXTILES \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (c):-  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\n  \n \n \nStatement referred to in reply to the Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *202 asked by Shri Arjun \nSingh to be answered on 21.12.2022 regarding Scheme To Promote Jute Industry \n \n(a) & (b):  The Government of India is implementing an Umbrella Program namely National Jute \nDevelopment Program (NJDP) with an outlay of Rs. 485.58 crore for overall development and \npromotion of jute sector including jute industry during the period of 2021-22 to 2025-26.  \n \nNJDP comprises of following schemes.: \n1. JUTE-ICARE (Improved Cultivation And Advanced Retting Exercise) Scheme \n2. Jute Diversification Scheme (JDS) \n3. Market Development & Promotion Scheme (MDPS) \n4. Scholarship Scheme for Girl Children of Workers of Jute Mills/MSME JDP unit \n \nAlso, the Government has given mandate to Jute Corporation of India Ltd. for procurement of raw jute \nunder MSP operation to safeguard the farmers from distress sale. Further, the Government by \nmandating reservation norms under the Jute Pac kaging Material (Compulsory Use in Packaging \nCommodities) Act, 1987, seeks to protect the interest of farmers and workers involved in the jute \nindustry.  \n \n(c): Does not arise in view of reply to part (a). \n*** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_203": "1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS  \n DEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 203  \nFOR ANSWER ON 21st DECEMBER, 2022  \n \nFREE INTERNET FACILITY \n       \n†*203.  SHRIMATI SHARDABEN ANILBHAI PATEL: \n  SHRI MITESH RAMESHBHAI PATEL (BAKABHAI): \n  \n Will the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether a large number of people in the  country are not being able to use free internet \nfacility and are unable to get online facility; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto; \n \n(c)  whether the Government proposes to provide free internet facility to those people who have \nno access to internet facility; and \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the time by which free internet facility is likely to be provided \nin various parts of the country? \n  \nANSWER  \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS & \n ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n \n\n2 \n \nSTATEMENT TO BE LAID ON THE TABLE OF LOK SABHA IN RESPECT OF PARTS \n(a) to (d) OF LOK SABHA  STARRED QUESTION NO. 203 FOR 21 st DECEMBER, 2022 \nREGARDING “FREE INTERNET FACILITY” \n \n(a) to (d)    As per “The Indian Telecom Services Performance Indicators”, report released by \nTelecom Regulatory Authority of India (TRAI) on 23rd November, 2022 there were total 836.86 \nmillion internet subscribers in the country as on 30th June, 2022 which is 60.73 In ternet \nSubscribers per 100 population. \n \nLicensees with Internet Service Provider (ISP) License / Authorization and  Public Data \nOffice Aggregators (PDOAs) registered under the Pradhan Mantri WiFi Access Network Interface \n(PM WANI) framework, have been permi tted to provide Internet Service as per the License \nconditions / PM WANI framework respectively based on their techno commercial considerations. \nPresently there is no proposal under consideration of the Ministry for providing free internet \nfacility. \n \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_204": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.204 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nCONSTRUCTION WORK OF RUB \n \n*204. SHRI KANUMURU RAGHU RAMA KRISHNA RAJU:        \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Ministry has any plans of taking up the construction work \nof Railway Under Bridge (RUB) at LC No. 27 situated near \nNarasapuram railway station in the coming financial year, if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n(b) whether any budget estimates have been prepared to include in the \nensuing budget for allocating sufficient funds for this RUB; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (c):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 204 BY SHRI KANUMURU RAGHU RAMA KRISHNA RAJU  \nTO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 21.12.2022 REGARDING \nCONSTRUCTION WORK OF RUB \n \n(a) to (c): Presently, there is no Level Crossing near Narasapuram. Level \nCrossing ( LC) No. 27 at Km. 28/9 -29/0 in Narasapuram station yard \n(Terminal station) on Bhimavaram -Narasapuram section was closed in \nAugust, 2021 with consent from District Collector b y providing a \ndiversion road.  Moreover, Road Under Bridge (RUB) at this location is \ntechnically not feasible due to less bank height, high water table and \nmajor irrigation canal and drain passing nearby. There is no plan for \nconstruction of any RUB at this location. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_205": "1 \n \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution \nDepartment of Consumer Affairs \n \nLOK  SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *205 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \n \nPROTECTION OF CONSUMER RIGHTS FOR ONLINE PURCHASE \n \n*205. SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to protect the rights of consumers purchasing goods \nthrough online and if so, the details of action taken thereon;  \n(b)  whether the Government proposes to amend the Consumer Protection Law for ensuring \nprotection of rights of consumers in e-commerce and if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Government proposes to initiate action for ensuring warranty offered by the \ncompanies to the consumers and if so, the action taken thereon;  \n (d)  whether it has come to the notice of the Government that online service centers and \nmanufacturers of the goods are not providing receipts to the complaints lodged by the \nconsumers and failed to provide the service as agreed and if so, the action taken by the \nGovernment to protect the rights of consumers; and  \n(e)  whether the Government proposes to make dealers and retailers also liable for ensuring \nwarranty and if so, the action taken thereon? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h  \n¼Jh ih;w\"k xks;y½ \n \nTHE MINISTER OF  \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n  (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (e)  :   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n***** \n \n \n \n \n\n2 \n \n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO  (e) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.* 205 FOR 21.12.2022 REGARDING \nPROTECTION OF CONSUMER RIGHTS FOR ONLINE PURCHASE. \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n \n(a), (b) & (d): To protect the rights of consumers purchasing goods through  e-commerce, the \nCentral Government has notified the Consumer Protection (E -commerce) Rules, 2020. The rules \nwere notified and came into force on 23rd July, 2020. \n \nThe rules have been notified under Section 101(zg) read with Section 94 of the Consumer \nProtection Act, 2019 wherein the Central Government has been empowered to take such \nmeasures as may be prescribed for the purposes of preventing unfair trade practices in e -\ncommerce and to protect the interest and rights of consumers. \n \nThe rules prescribe the duties of e-commerce entities, liabilities of marketplace e-commerce \nentities, d uties of sellers on marketplace and d uties and liabilities of inventory e -commerce \nentities, which inter-alia include: \ni. Prominent display to users, in a clear and accessible man ner on its platform – legal \nname, geographic address of its headquarters and all branches, contact details like e -\nmail address, landline and mobile numbers of customer care as well as of grievance \nofficer \nii. Establish adequate grievance redressal mechanism ha ving regard to the number of \ngrievances and appoint a grievance officer for consumer grievance redressal. The \ngrievance officer is required to acknowledge the receipt of any consumer complaint \nwithin 48 hours and redress the complaint within 1 month. \niii. In ca se of offering imported goods for sale, mention the name and details of any \nimporter from whom it has purchased such goods or services, or who may be a seller on \nits platform. \niv. To effect all payments of accepted refund requests of the consumers as prescribe d by \nthe RBI or any other competent authority under any law for the time being in force, \nwithin a reasonable period of time, or as prescribed under applicable laws. \nv. Not to adopt any unfair trade practice, whether in the course of business on its platform \nor otherwise. \nFurther, t he Department of Consumer Affairs operates a National Consumer Helpline \n(NCH) wherein the consumer can lodge their grievances. The NCH acts as a pre -litigation \nmechanism which receives grievances of consumers through telephone (short  code 1915), web \nportal, letters, SMS, emails etc. and Mobile App. These grievances are  then taken up with the \nconcerned entities for resolution. \n  \n\n3 \n \n \n \nAll the complaints lodged with NCH are acknowledged through a docket number. \n \n(c) & (e) :  Giving to the p ublic any warranty or guarantee of the performance, efficacy or \nlength of life of a product or of any goods that is not based on an adequate or proper test thereof \nconstitutes an ‘unfair trade practice’ under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019. The Act also \nprovides for a product liability action against product manufacturers, product sellers and product \nservice providers. \n \nA product manufacturer shall be held liable if the product does not conform to the express \nwarranty even if he proves that he was not negligent or fraudulent in making the express \nwarranty of a product. \n \nA product seller shall be liable where he has made an express warranty of a product \nindependent of any express warranty made by a manu facturer and such product fails  to conform \nto the express warranty made by the product seller.  \n \nA product service provider shall be liable for a product liability action, if the service did \nnot conform to the express warranty or the terms and conditions of the contract. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_206": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.206 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07-12-2022 \n  \nINSTALMENTS OF MPLAD SCHEME \n  \n 206. SHRI RAJIV RANJAN SINGH ALIAS LALAN SINGH: \n        SHRI DINESH CHANDRA YADAV: \n        SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR: \n  \n           \nWill the Minister of STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the number of instalments released under MPLAD Scheme after the \ncorona (COVID) period; \n(b) whether MPLAD scheme has been restored as earlier, if so, the \ndetails thereof;  \n(c) whether the release of instalments under MPLAD Scheme has been \ndelayed in many Parliamentary Constituencies due to non-availability of \nfunds to be released by the Union Government; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n  \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF \nSTATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION, MINISTER OF \nSTATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF PLANNING AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS (RAO \nINDERJIT SINGH) \n  \n(a) & (b)   The MPLAD Scheme was non -operational for two financial \nyears 2020-21 & 2021-22 for managing the economic and health impacts \nof COVID-19 pandemic and same has been restored in accordance with \nthe decision taken by the Union Cabinet in its meeting held  on 10-11-\n2021, for the remaining part of the Financial Year 2021 -22 with release \nof MPLADS fund at the rate of ₹ 2 crore per Member of Parliament in one \n\ninstalment and continued MPLAD Scheme up to 2025 -26 with annual \nentitlement per Member of Parliament ( MP) at ₹ 5 crores. After \nrestoration of the Scheme, the Ministry has released 1199 instalments \ntill 30.11.2022. \n  \n(c) & (d)    Release of funds under MPLADS is strictly subject to \nfulfillment of fund -related criteria and submission of fund -related \ndocuments by District Authorities as prescribed under extant MPLADS \nGuidelines. Instalments under MPLADS have been released by the \nMinistry of Statistics and Programme Implementation in all cases \nfulfilling the said criteria.  \n \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_207": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COAL \n  \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *207 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21/12/2022 \n  \nUNDER-UTILISATION OF COAL MINES \n  \n*207. SHRI DR. A. CHELLAKUMAR: \n SHRI BENNY BEHANAN: \n  \nWill the Minister of  COAL be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government has examined or intends to examine the issue of under -utilisation of \nexisting coal mines;; \n  \n(b) if so, the details thereof including measures taken to address the afore -mentioned issue of \nunder-utilization; and; \n  \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS, COAL AND MINES \n (SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI) \n  \n(a) to (c):  A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n  \n**** \n  \n  \n  \n\nStatement in Reply to the Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 207 to be answered on 21.12.2022 \nregarding Under-utilization of Coal Mines  \n  \n(a) to (c): Coal mines are operated as per approved mining plans and coal productions are \nmonitored against the level given in the mining plan for that part icular year. Coal mines are \nrunning on an average at optimal capacity as per mining plans. Considering last 5 years average, \nCIL's overall system capacity utilization is near about 80%. The capacity utilization of SCCL has \nbeen near about 82 -90% and capacity utilization of NLCIL has been near about 85% - 100% as \nper mine plan. Operations of coal mines are monitored by the Government on regular basis.  \n  \n  \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_208": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.208 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF ROBs IN BIHAR \n \n208.  DR. SANJAY JAISWAL:         \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways has taken up projects to construct Railway \nOver Bridges (ROBs) in the State of Bihar and if so, the details \nthereof; \n(b) whether it is true that the projects shall be taken up in collaboration \nwith the State Government of Bihar and if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the details of the division of work and investments to be made \nbetween the Central and the State Government of Bihar in this \nregard; and \n(d) the progress of such projects along with the time by which the \nprojects are likely to be completed? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n(a) & (b):  Yes, Sir.  82 Nos. of Railway Over Bridge (ROBs) have been \nsanctioned on cost sharing basis with State Govt. of Bihar.  The details of \nthese works are as under:   \n(i) 03 Nos. of ROBs work assigned to Railway on single entity basis. \n(ii) 13 Nos. of ROBs assigned  jointly with State Govt. \n(iii) 06 Nos. of ROBs work assigned  to DFCCIL and 01 ROB by IRCON. \n\n(iv) 59 Nos. of ROBs work assigned to State Govt of Bihar on single \nentity basis.  \n(c):  Total investment of these 82 ROBs is `3226.94 crore (Railway share  \n`1511.57 crore and  State share  `1715.37 crore). \n(d): Construction of ROBs involves sanction of work by State Government, \nfixing of alignment, shifting of utilities, acquisition of land etc. jointly \nbetween State Govt. and Railway.  Since, most of the ROBs (59 Nos.) work \nare assigned to State Govt of Bihar on single entity basis,  completion will \ndepend on various factors as elaborated above & action taken mostly by \nState Govt.  and availability of funds. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_209": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 209 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 07.12.2022 \n \nCHINESE APPLICATIONS UNDER USAGE \n  \n209:      SHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB: \n \nWill the Minister of ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) the number of chinese applications currently under usage and download in India after \nthe ban of a total 54 chinese apps along with the impact assessment report of the said \nban; \n \n(b) whether the Government is aware that multiple chinese applications are currently \nunder usage and are already more popular than multiple Indian applications; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI RAJEEV CHANDRASEKHAR) \n \n \n(a) to (c): Based on the request received from Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA), the \nMinistry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY) issued blocking directions to \nblocka total of 348 mobile applications including chinese application under the provisio n of \nsection 69A of the Information Technology (IT) Act, 2000 and the Information Technology \n(Procedure and Safeguards for Blocking for Access of Information for Public) Rules, 2009. \n \nThese mobile applications were blocked in the interest of sovereignty and integrity of India, \ndefense of India and security of the State. \n \nThe database of mobile applications available on internet  is not maintained by this ministry. \nThe mobile applications that were blocked under section 69Aare not operational in India. \n \n******* \n  \n\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_21": "1 \n \n������������������� �\n�������������������������� �\n�������������� ������������������ �\n�\n��������� �\n����������������������� ���\n������������������ ��� ���������������� �\n�\n���������������������� �\n�\n����������� ������������������� �\n��������������������� �\n������������������� �\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� �����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ��� ���� ���� �������� ������������������ ���� ������� �������� ������ ����� ���� ��������� ������ ������ ��� ����\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������\n�\n����� ��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n�\n����� ������������������������������� �\n����������������������� �\n�\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������� �������� �������� ���� ���������� ������� ��������� ������������� ��� ���� ���������� ��������� ��� ����\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������ �����������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������� �����\n�\n����������� ����������� ���� ������������ ���� �������� ��� ������� ��������� �������� ������ ������ ����\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n\n2 \n \n�������� ����\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������