� �� ������� ��� ������������������������ ���������� ����� ��������� ������������� ����\n�������������������������������������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����� �������� ���� �� ������� ��� ������ ������������� ����� ������� �������� ������ ������������ ���\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n��������\n� �\n\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_211": "�\n��������� �\n�������������������������� �\n����������������������� ������\n�\n�\n�\n�\n����������������������������� �\n�\n�\n����������������������� �\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n���������������������������������������������\n����������������������\n�\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n�\n�\n�������\n������ �\n������������� ������������������������������������������������\n���������������������� ��� ���������� �\n����������������������� ��\n�\n����� ������ ���� ��� ������ ������ ��������� �������� ������������ ����� ���������������� ����� ��������� �����\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����������� ����������� ��������� ��� ���� �������� ����������� �������������� ������������ ��������� ����\n����������� ��������� �������� ��� ���� �������� ������ ����������������� ������� ��������������� �����������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����\n�\n��\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_212": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 212 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nNEW RAILWAY PROJECTS IN MADHYA PRADESH \n \n†*212. SHRI UDAY PRATAP SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is working on any plan to start a new \nrailway project in Madhya Pradesh, if so, the details thereof and the \ntime by which it is likely to be implemented; \n(b) whether the Government has received any demand/proposal from \nthe State Government in this regard, if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether operations of many trains were discontinued and the \nschedules of many trains were modified due to Corona pandemic in \nMadhya Pradesh, if so, the details of th trains which have not been \nre-started so far; \n(d) whether the Governme nt has carried out any assessment for \nestimation of lo sses incurred due to discontina tion of the said \ntrains, if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) the measures taken/likely to be taken by the Government in this \nregard? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*****  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 212 BY SHRI UDAY PRATAP SINGH TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 21.12.2022 REGARDING  NEW RAILWAY PROJECTS IN \nMADHYA PRADESH \n \n(a) and (b): Railway projects are sanctioned Zonal Railway -wise, not \nState-wise, as Indian Railways’ projects may span across various State \nboundaries. \n  \n  Proposals/suggestions/representations, both formal and informal, \nincluding that from Hon’ble Members of Parliament are received at \nvarious levels of Railway Administration viz. Division, Zonal Headquarter \nand Railway Board’s level for introduction of new lines, Ga uge \nconversion, Doubling etc., a compendium of which is not maintained. \nHowever, these are examined and action as found feasible and justified \nis taken from time to time.  \n \nAs on 01.04.2022, 33 Railway projects (08 new lines, 02 gauge \nconversion and 23 dou bling), costing `84,469 crore for 5,872 km length, \nfalling fully/partly in Madhya Pradesh are  under different stages of \nplanning/approval/execution. Out of which, 1,319 km length has been \ncommissioned and an expenditure of `23,780 crore has been incurred \nupto March 2022. These include: \n \n 08 New Line Projects covering total length of 1,979 km at a cost of \n`36,163  crore, out of which 355 km length has been commissioned \nand an expenditure of `6,606 crore has been incurred upto March \n22.  \n 02 Gauge Conversion Projects covering total length of 780 km at a \ncost of `10,764 crore, out of which 279 km length has been \ncommissioned and an expenditure of `3,015 crore has been \nincurred upto March 22. \n…P/2 \n\n-:2:- \n 23 Doubling Projects covering total length of 3,113 km at a cost of \n`37,542 crore, out of which 685 km length has been commissioned \nand an expenditure of `14,159 crore has been incurred upto March \n22. \n \nPresently, 29 Nos. of Surveys (12 New Line and 17 Doub ling) falling \nfully/partly in the State of Madhya Pradesh having a total length of 2842 \nKm have been taken up and are in different stages of progress. \n \nRailway projects in Madhya Pradesh are covered by North Central \nRailway, North Western Railway, West Cen tral Railway, East Central \nRailway, Western Railway, Central Railway, South Central Railway and \nSouth East Central Railway Zones of Indian Railways. The details of \nRailway projects including allotment of funds and expenditure, project -\nwise and Zonal Railwa y wise are made available in public domain on \nIndian Railways website i.e. www.indianrailways.gov.in> Ministry of \nRailways> Railway Board> About Indian Railways>Railway Board \nDirectorates> Finance (Budget), Pink Book (year)>Railway wise Works \nMachinery & Rolling Stock Programme. \n \n Since 2014, there has been substantial increase in Budget \nallotment for infrastructure projects. Average annual Budget allocation \nfor infrastructure projects and safety works, falling fully/partly i n the \nState of Madhya Pradesh, during 2014 -19 has been enhanced to `4,213 \ncrore per year from `632 crore per year during 2009 -14, which is 567% \nmore than average annual Budget allocation during 2009 -14. Annual \nBudget all ocations on these projects have been increased to `6,906 \ncrore in Financial Year 2019 -20 (993% more than average annual Budget \nallocation of 2009-14), `6,509 crore in Financial Year 2020-21(930% more \n…P/3 \n\n-:3:- \nthan the average annual Budget allocation of 2009 -14) and `9,041 crore \nin Financial Year 2021 -22 (1331% more than the average annual Budget \nallocation of 2009 -14). For Financial Year 2022 -23, the highest ever \nBudget allocation of `12,110 crore has been provide d for these projects, \nwhich is 1816% more than the average annual Budget allocation of 2009 -\n14 (`632 crore per year). \n \nDuring 2014-22, 1515 km sections (293 km New line, 631 km Gauge \nconversion and 591 km Doubling ), falling fully/partly in the S tate of  \nMadhya Pradesh, have been commissioned at an average rate of 189.38 \nkm per year, which is 553% more than average annual commissioning \nachieved during 2009-14 (29 km per year). \n \nCompletion of Railway project/s depends on various factors like \nquick land acquisition by State Government, forest clearance by officials \nof forest department, shifting of infringing utilities, statutory clearances \nfrom various authorities, geological and topographical conditions of \narea, law and order situation in the area of projec t/s site, number of \nworking months in a year for particular project site etc. All these factors \naffect the completion time of the project/s.  With above constraints, \nevery effort is being made to execute the project/s expeditiously. \n \n(c) to (e): With a vie w to contain the spread of Covid -19 pandemic, Indian \nRailways had discontinued the operation  of all regular passenger \ncarrying trains with effect from 23rd March, 2020 and only special train \nservices were being operated. Indian Railways have also undertake n \nrationalization of time table, including rationalization of train services, in \na scientific manner with the assistance of IIT-Bombay. The exercise has \nbeen undertaken inter alia to provide for better passenger safety by  \n…P/4 \n\n-:4:- \ncreating maintenance corridor blocks, minimizing conflicts in existing \ntime table to improve punctuality and generation of additional path for \nfreight traffic. At present, all train services are being operated as per the \nrationalized time table and passenger servi ces are being operated in \nphased manner.  However, Indian Railways do not run train services on \nState-wise basis as R ailway network straddle across S tate boundaries.  \nTrain-wise figures of losses are not maintained.  \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_213": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No.213 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF RAIL LINE BETWEEN JAGDALPUR AND ROWGHAT  \n \n†*213. SHRI DEEPAK BAIJ:  \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Bhoomi Pujan of the Jagdalpur – Rowghat - Dallirajhara \nRailway line project was done on 28 September 2018;    \n \n(b) if so, the current status of the said Railway line; \n \n(c) the status of construction of Jagdalpur -Rowghat Railway line so far; \nand \n \n(d) the time by which the said project is likely to be completed alongwith \nthe details of progress in this direction? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY   \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n  \n(a) to (d) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n                                                      \n*****          \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO.  213 BY SHRI DEEPAK BAIJ TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK \nSABHA ON  21.12.2022 REGARDING CONSTRUCTION OF RAIL LINE \nBETWEEN JAGDALPUR AND ROWGHAT \n \n(a) to (d) : Yes, Sir. The bhoomi pujan for Jagdalpur – Rowghat portion of \nDallirajhara – Rowghat – Jagdalpur Railway line project was done on 28 -\n12-2018. The Railway has taken up construction of Dallirajhara – Rowghat \n- Jagdalpur rail line (235 Km) project in two phases. The Phase -I of the \nproject is from Dallirajhara to Rowghat (0 - 95 km) and the Phase-II of the \nproject is from Rowghat to Jagdalpur (95 - 235 km). The Phase -I of the \nproject between Dallirajhara - Rowghat (95km) is being executed by Rail \nVikas Nigam Limited (RVNL) through funding by Steel Authority of India \nLimited (SAIL) and the Phase -II of the project between Rowghat - \nJagdalpur (140 km) h as been planned for execution through Special \nPurpose Vehicle (SPV) named Bastar Railway Private Limited (BRPL) \nconsisting of Government of Chhattisgarh, SAIL, National Mineral \nDevelopment Corporation (NMDC) and IRCON. The present status of the \nproject is as under:  \n \n(i) Phase-I Dallirajhara - Rowghat (95 km) : This section is being \nexecuted by RVNL and funded by SAIL. The latest anticipat ed cost \nof the project is ` 1622 Crore. Work on this section was started in \n2010. The work from Dallirajhara to Antagarh  (60 Km) has been \ncompleted. The work has been taken up in balance section. Project \nArea is in problem affected area and work has to be taken up under \ndedicated security cover with daily mobilization and demobilization \nif mechanism is required. This is aff ecting the pace of execution of \nthe project. Completion of any Railway project(s) depends on \nvarious factors like quick land acquisition by State Government, \nforest clearance by officials of forest department, shifting of \ninfringing  utilities,  statutory  clearances  from  various  authorities, \n \nCont…2/.. \n\n-:2:- \n \ngeological and topographical conditions of area,  law and order \nsituation in the area of project/s site, number of working months in \na year for particular project/s site etc. All these factors affect the \ncompletion time of the project/s . With above constraints, Railway is \nmaking all effort for expeditious completion of project(s). \n \n(ii) Phase-II - Rowghat - Jagdalpur (140 Km) : The land acquisition for \nthis Phase is under process and approximately 249 Ha of land out of \n776 Ha required for the project has been acquired. The balance land \nyet to be acquired constitutes of 527 Ha consisting of 95 Ha of \nprivate land and 432 Ha of forest land. The Phase-II of the project is \nscheduled to be completed wi thin four years after the land \nacquisition and financial closure of the project. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_214": "  \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *214 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nNEW TEXTILE PARKS \n \n*214. SHRI PARTHIBAN S.R.: \n \n \n Will the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंत्री \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether any new textile park is proposed to be set up in Tamil Nadu;  \n \n(b) if so, the district-wise details of places where such parks are proposed to be set up; and  \n \n(c) the details of the estimated number of people who will get employment after setting up of \nthese parks? \n  \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र मंत्री (श्री पीयूष गोयल) \nMINISTER OF TEXTILES \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (c):-  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\n  \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (c) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *214 DUE FOR ANSWER ON 21.12.2022 RAISED BY \nSHRI PARTHIBAN S.R REGARDING NEW TEXTILE PARKS. \n \n(a) to (c): The Union Cabinet has approved setting up of 7 PM Mega Integrated Textile \nRegions and Apparel (PM MITRA) Parks across the country with a total budgetar y outlay of \nRs.4,445 Crore. Under the scheme, 18 proposals from 13 state governments including Tamil \nNadu have been received. The final selection of sites is at an advanced stage. O nce completed, \neach such Mega Textile Park is expected to generate direct e mployment for about 1 lakh \npersons and indirect employment for about 2 lakh persons. \n \n*** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_215": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.215 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF RUBs/ROBs \n \n215.  SHRI NARANBHAI KACHHADIYA:  \nSHRI PARBATBHAI SAVABHAI PATEL:         \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of representations received by the Railways for \nconstruction of Rail Under -Bridges(RUBs)/ Rail Over Bridges \n(ROBs) in Amreli and Banaskantha Districts; \n(b) the progress made thereon on these representations; and \n(c) the time by which the sanctioned RUBs/ROBs are likely to be \ncompleted? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n(a) to (c):  Yes, Sir.   \nAmerli: 01 representation for construction of Road Over Bridge (ROB) \nalongwith Road Under Bridge (RUB) in lieu of Level Crossing (LC) No. 17 \nin Amreli -Khizidia section and 01 ROB on bypass at Sabarkantha city \nhas been received.  These works are being executed by  Road and \nBuilding department (R&B), Govt. of Gujarat.  RUB in lieu of LC No. 17 \nhas been constructed and commissioned.  Work is in progress at both \nbalance ROBs by R&B department, Govt. Of Gujarat.  \n \n\nBanaskantha: 06 Nos. of representation for construction of ROB/RUB \nhave been received in Banaskantha district.   \n(i) LC No. 159 (having Traffic Vehicle Unit (TVU – 180985)  at Km. \n212/9-213/0 on Samdari -Bhildi section. As per extant policy, the \nwork for construction of R OB is considered by Railway as per \npriority and availability of funds subject to consent providing of \nencumbrance free land at its own cost for approaches and \nclosure of LC after construction of ROB.  However, if State Govt. \ndesires to construct ROB at thi s location early, it can be \nconsidered on deposit terms.   \n(ii) LC No. 143 at Km 616/8-9 on Ajmer Palanpur section.  This LC was \nclosed by construction of subway in its lieu in May 2021 with \nconsent from District Authority.  At present, there is no LC.  \nHowever,  ROB at this location can be considered on deposit \nterms provided State Government agrees to bear 100% cost of \nconstruction and maintenance subject to its feasibility. No \nProposal in this regard is received from State Government. \n(iii) LC No. 171A (having TVU-9038 (Palanpur-Ahmedabad): RUB in lieu \nof LC No. 171A has been sanctioned and work is in progress and \nlikely to be completed in 2023-24.  \n(iv) LC No. 167B (Palanpur-Karjoda): This LC was closed with consent \nfrom District Magistrate due to low Traffic Vehicle Un it (TVU).  At \npresent there is no LC.  However, ROB at this location can be \nconsidered on deposit terms provided State Government agrees \nto bear 100% cost of construction and maintenance subject to its \nfeasibility. No P roposal in this regard is received fr om State \nGovernment. \n(v) LC No. 26 (Palanpur-Samakhiali): This LC falls on Special Purpose \nVehicle (SPV) line of Pipavav Railway Corporation Ltd. (PRCL).  \n\nAny work on these lines can be done by PRCL or State Govt./Road \nOwing Authority at their own cost.   \n(vi) LC No. 62 (having TVU  - 197077 (Palanpur-Samakhiali): ROB work \nin lieu of LC No. 62 has been sanctioned and work is in progress \nand likely to be completed in 2023-24. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_216": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 216 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nUPGRADATION OF RAILWAY STATIONS IN MMR \n*216. SHRI MANOJ KOTAK: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n   \n(a) whether the Government is planning to upgrade all railway stations \nof Mumbai Metropolitan Region (MMR); \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the time by which the said project is likely to commence; \n(d) whether the number of platforms will be increased while carr ying \nout the renovation work of railway stations; and \n(e) if so, the numb er of new platforms to be built  and the amount \nestimated to be spent on the said project? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW)  \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) O F \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 216 BY SHRI MANOJ KOTAK  TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 21.12.2022 REGARDING UPGRADATION \nOF RAILWAY STATIONS IN MMR \n(a) to (c ): Upgradation and Modernisation of railway stations and \namenities is a continuous and ongoing process on Indian Railways. \nMinistry of Railways is also undertaking techno -economic feasibility \nstudies for redevelopment of S tations. Based on the outcome of these \nfeasibility studies, stations are planned to be taken up for \nredevelopment in phases, especially the stations located in major \ncities and important tourist destination.  So far, Chhatrapati Shivaji \nMaharaj Terminus (CSMT), Thane and Mumbai Central have been \nidentified for redevelopment based on such studies in Mumbai \nMetropolitan Region  (MMR). Thakurli and Lokmanya Tilak Terminus  \nRailway Stations have also been identified for such studies in MMR. \n Apart fro m the above, 9  Stations viz. Bhandup, Mulund, \nDombivali, Neral, Ghatkopar, GTB Nagar, Chembur, Govandi and \nMankhurd of Central Railway and 7 Stations Viz. Khar Road, Santacruz, \nKandivali, Mira Road , Bhayandar, Vasai Road and Na llasopara of \nWestern Railway are being taken up for improvement under MUTP-IIIA. \nUpgradation/Development of Railway Stations at this scale is \ncomplex in nature and requires detailed techno -economic feasibility \nstudies and various statutory clearances from urban/local bodies etc. \nand these factors affect the completion time. Therefore, no time -frame \ncan be indicated. \n(d) & (e): Planning of additional platforms depends upon the availability \nof space and number of passenger s dealt at that station.  Three New \nplatforms are being built at K har Road, Chembur and GTB Nagar \nStations (one each). The estimated amount to be spent in MUTP -IIIA \nfor improvement of 18 stations is ₹  1053 crore. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_217": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n   LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  217 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE PROJECTS \n \n217   SHRI E.T. MOHAMMED BASHEER: \n \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has prepared comprehensive projects \nfor the development of port  and railway connectivity,  if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n(b) whether Kerala is included in the same project; and  \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \n ELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \n \n     (SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a)� Yes, Sir. Ministry of Ports, Shipping, and Waterways, Ministry of \nRailways, Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, and DPIIT \nhave jointly finalized a comprehensive ac tion plan for port \nconnectivity.  \nUnder Sagarmala Projects for Rail Connectivity with Port, 20 \nprojects have been completed.  \n(b)&(c)Yes, Sir. Kochi and Vallarpadam Ports are already connected to \nrail network with adequate capacity.  \nFor Azhikkal  Port-Fishing Harbour, t he volume of traffic is very \nlow. Rail Connectivity is not required. \nOn date, there is no project for Kollam & Beypore Ports.  \n                                         ******�",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_218": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 218 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nTRI-WEEKLY SERVICE OF OKHA-HARIDWAR EXPRESS \n \n*218. SHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJI KUNDARIYA:   \n  \n    Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether a proposal has been received by the Ministry for operating \nof train no. 19565/66  Okha-Haridwar express, between Okha -Delhi \nSarai Rohilla tri weekly, if so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether it is a fact that inspite of tremendous public demand o f \npeople of Saurashtra the proposal has been kept at abeyance; \n(c) if so, the reasons for the same; and \n(d) the time likely to be taken for implementation of the proposal? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n (SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW)  \n \n \n(a) to (d)  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 218 BY SHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJI \nKUNDARIYA TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 21.12.2022 \nREGARDING TRI-WEEKLY SERVICE OF OKHA-HARIDWAR EXPRESS \n \n(a) to (d) Yes, Sir. Requests, including from the Hon’ble Member of \nParliament, have been received for increase in frequency of 19565/66 \nOkha-Dehradun Express  from weekly  to tri -weekly. The matter has \nbeen examined but not found feasible, at present, due to operational \nconstraints including terminal constraints at both ends and path \nconstraints on sections enroute.   However, increase in frequency of \ntrain services depends on operational feasibility, resource availability, \ntraffic justification, etc., which is an on-going process. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_219": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  219 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2022 \n \nKISAN RAIL SCHEME \n \n \n*219.   SHRI THOMAS CHAZHIKADAN: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether  the Government is planning to include the raw \nmaterials used for producti on of cattle feed in the Kisan Rail \nScheme; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) & (b) :  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n******** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) AND (b) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 219 BY SHRI THOMAS CHAZHIKADAN TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 21.12.2022 REGARDING KISAN \nRAIL SCHEME \n \n(a):   No, Sir. \n \n(b):    Does not arise.   \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_22": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 22\n(To be answered on the 8th December 2022)\n \nSUGGESTIONS TO IMPROVE AIR TRAVEL\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether suggestions are received through the website of the Ministry of\nCivil Aviation especially with reference to the announcement made during the\nair journey inviting suggestions to make the air travel more comfortable and\nif so, the details thereof; and\n(b) the details of the number of suggestions received including the number of\nsuggestions implemented so far?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (b) A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n*****\n*22. SHRI JAGANNATH SARKAR\n be pleased to state:-\n (Shri Jyotiraditya M. Scindia)\n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION\nNUMBER 22 FOR 8th DECEMBER 2022\n \n \n(a) and (b) Yes Sir. The Air Sewa Portal operated by the Ministry of Civil\nAviation (MoCA) is used for redressal of complaints of air passengers.\nComplaints received through Air Sewa Portal are monitored by the Air Sewa\nCell in the Ministry for their redressal in a time bound manner. Some of these\ncomplaints also contains suggestions. All such complaints and suggestions are\nshared with the concerned airline, airports or stakeholder.\n \nDuring the period of April-November 2022, 6755 complaints/suggestions were\nreceived of which 6671 complaints/suggestions have been addressed.\n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_220": "��\n�\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 220 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7TH DECEMBER, 2022 \n \nNUMBER OF VILLAGES NOT CONNECTED WITH INTERNET \n \n220.  SHRI UPENDRA SINGH RAWAT:  \nSHRI BHOLANATH (B.P. SAROJ):  \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  the details of the number of villages which are not connected with internet services in the \ncountry especially in Uttar Pradesh;  \n \n(b)  the time by which each and every village in the country is expected to get internet \nconnectivity;  \n \n(c)  the details of the funds allocated/released/utilized and financial assistance given by the \nGovernment during the last three years and the current year for the said purpose, State/UT- wise \nparticularly in the State of UP;  \n \n(d)  the steps taken by the Government to increase digital literacy in rural areas; and  \n \n(e)  the details of the funds allocated and the financial assistance given by the Government \nduring the last three years and the current year to increase digital literacy?    \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR COMMUNICATIONS \n(SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN) \n \n(a) to (c)  As per data provided from Telecom Service Providers (TSPs), Department of \nTelecom field unit and State Government as of March '2022, out of 6,44,131 villages (villages are \nas per data of Registrar General of India as of November 2019), around 6,05,230 number of \nvillages are having mobile internet connectivity in the country and 38901 villages are not having \nmobile connectivity. In the State of Uttar Pradesh out of 105531 villages, 1,05,257 number of \nvillages are connected with mobile internet and 274 villages are not having any mobile \nconnectivity. Government and Telecom Service Providers (TSPs) provide telecommunication \nconnectivity in the country in a phased manner. Government through funding from Universal \nService Obligation Fund (USOF) is implementing various schemes for providing mobile internet \nconnectivity in all remaining villages of the country. Around Rs 18419.20 Cr. have been disbursed \nfrom USOF in last three years and current financial year up to October 2022 in the country \nincluding the State of Uttar Pradesh. \n\n��\n�\n(d) & (e)  To increase the digital literacy in the rural areas, Government of India has approved \n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\ndigital literacy in rural India by covering 6 crore rural households (one person per household). To \nensure equitable geographical reach, each of the 2,50,000 Gram Panchayats across the country are \nenvisaged to register an average of 200- 300 candidates. As on 2nd December 2022, a total of around \n6.59 crore candidates have been enrolled and 5.66 crore have been trained, out of which 4.21 crore \ncandidates have been certified under the PMGDISHA Scheme.  During the last three yeas viz. \n2019- 20 , 2020- 21 and 2021- 22, an amount of Rs.400 crore, Rs. 250 crore and Rs. 300 crore were \nreleased respectively for the PMGDISHA Scheme. During the current financial year i.e. 2022- 23, \nRs. 250 Crore has been allocated for the said scheme.      \n******* ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_221": "������������������� �\n������������������������������� �\n������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n�\n����������������������� ��� ��\n����������������������������������� �� ��������� ��������\n�\n���� �\n�\n������ �������������������������������� �\n�\n������������������������������������������ ����������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����� ������������������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����� ����������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������\n�\n����� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������� ��\n�\n������ �\n�\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������ �\n������������������ �\n�\n������ ������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� ������ ������������������ ������� ��� ��� ���� ����� ��� �������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� �������������� ���������������������� ������ �������� ������������ ���������������������� ������ �������������������� ���������� ��������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��