    "ls|LS17_S10_U_222": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 222\n(To be answered on the 22nd December 2022)\n \nDIGI YATRA FACILITY\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Government has introduced Digi Yatra for digital travel experience based on\nfacial biometrics on airports in the country and if so, the details thereof;\n \n(b) the names of airports in which such a facility is currently being provided, airport-wise;\n \n(c) the names of the domestic and international airlines which would provide Digi Yatra facility\nto the passengers in the country, airlines-wise;\n \n(d) whether the Government has developed a Digi Yatra app to facilitate the passengers and if\nso, the details thereof; and\n \n(e) the steps being taken by the Government to start Digi Yatra in all the airports across the\ncountry to facilitate the passengers and reduce the burden of cumbersome check-in and\nboarding process along with the time by which such facility would be operational? \n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (e) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n*****\n*222. SHRI PRATAPRAO JADHAV\nSHRI MANOJ TIWARI\n be pleased to state:-\n (Shri Jyotiraditya M. Scindia)\n\nStatement referred in the reply to Lok Sabha Starred (*) Question No. 222 for 22.12.2022\nregarding \"Digi Yatra\"\n \n(a) & (b) Yes, Sir. Digi Yatra has been launched on 01.12.2022 at Delhi, Bangalore and Varanasi\nAirports for providing passengers seamless and hassle-free experience based on facial\nbiometrics.\n \n(c) Digi Yatra Facility is only for domestic airlines. Presently, all domestic airlines at Delhi and\nBangalore Airports are providing this facility. At Varanasi Airport, the facility is currently\nprovided by Indigo, Vistara and Air India.\n \n(d) Yes, Sir. Digi Yatra App has been developed to facilitate the passengers. The same is\navailable on android as well as iOS platform.\n \n(e) The implementation of Digi Yatra under phase I is planned at Kolkata, Pune, Vijayawada\nand Hyderabad Airports by March 2023. It is to be implemented across various airports in the\ncountry in phased manner. \n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_223": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 223 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \nDOUBLING WORK OF JHANSI-MANIKPUR RAILWAY LINE  \n \n������������������������������������������������������ \n  \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the doubling work of Jhansi -Manikpur and Banda -Kanpur railway \nlines is being carried out under North Central Railway; \n(b) if so, the time by which the said work is likely to be started and  planned to \nbe completed; \n(c) whether the doubling work of Jhansi -Manikpur railway line under North -\nCentral Railway has already been taken up; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to  (d) Yes , Sir.  North Central Railway has taken up doubling of Jhansi -\nManikpur and Khairar -Bhimsen (425 Km).  Sanctioned Cost of project is �� 4330 \nCrore.  Works on the project have been taken up.  So far an expenditure of �� 151 \nCrore has been incurred on the  project.  An outlay of �� 400 Crore has been \nprovided for the project for financial year 2022-23.  \n \nThe completion of any Railway project(s) depends on various factors like quick \nland acquisition by State Government, forest clearance by officials of forest  \ndepartment, shifting of infringing utilities, statutory clearances from various \nauthorities, geological and topographical conditions of area, law and order \nsituation in the area of project(s) site, number of working months in a year for \nparticular project site due to climatic conditions etc. and all these factors affect \nthe completion time of the project(s).  With these constraints, Railways are \nmaking all efforts to complete these projects at the earliest. \n ***** �",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_224": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA                                                                                                            \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA                                                                                                                                 \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 224                                                                                                           \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \nK-RAIL (SILVERLINE) PROJECT \n \n224.  SHRI HIBI EDEN : \n \n          Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has noticed that without proper and legal \nsanction for the Silverline semi-high speed rail project, the Government of \nKerala is proceeding with the works of the same, if so, the facts and details \nthereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government of Kerala has submitted new amplifications or \nmagnifications for the K -Rail (Silverline) project for approval and permission, on \nor after 20.07.2022 and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Kerala Rail Development Corporation Limited (K -Rail) has not \nyet given technical documents and other details, including the alignment of the \nSilverline project, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the Government has re -examined or scrutinized the project on or \nafter 20.07.2022 and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(e) whether the consideration of the project is likely to depend upon soil \ncondition, natural drainage, env ironmental issues, interoperability, debt \nserviceability with mainly passenger traffic of the project, if so, the details of all \npre-conditions that may be considered before the Union Government grants \npermission/issue NOC; and \n \n(f) whether the Government is aware of the delay that occurred in issuing \npermission/NOC in the case of the K-Rail Silverline Project and if so, the stand of \nthe Government in this regard? \n \n \n   ANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \n ELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \n \n   (SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW)  \n \n(a) to (f): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*****  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f ) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 224 BY SHRI HIBI EDEN TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON \n07.12.2022 REGARDING K-RAIL (SILVER LINE) PROJECT. \n \n(a): No, Sir. Kerala Rail Development Corporation Ltd.(KRDCL) a Joint \nVenture Company of State Govt. of Kerala (51%) and Ministry of Railways \n(49%) has taken up the work of Silver Line (Semi High Speed Rail) from \nThiruvananthapuram to Kasaragod (530.6 Km.) for development. In Principle \nApproval (IPA) of Railway Board has been granted for this project for taking \nup pre-investment activities. Granting of IPA means go ahead for preparation \nof DPR etc which brings out the complete detail s of the project including \nfinancials. \n(b) to (d):  No, Sir. DPR is under examination by Ministry of Railways. \nSufficient details for technical feasibility are not available in the DPR. \nTherefore, KRDCL has been advised to provide detailed technical docume nts \nsuch as alignment plan, particulars of railway land and private land, \ncrossings over existing railway network, duly depicting affected railway \nasset through Zonal Railway for detailed examination of the project and to \narrive at conclusion about feasibi lity of project, which is awaited from \nKRDCL. \n(e): Financial viability will be examined and firmed up after finalisation of \ntechnical parameters. Consideration of the project will depend upon techno -\neconomic viability of the project. \n(f): The Project is no t yet sanctioned.  Therefore, question of delay does not \narise. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_225": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 225\n(To be answered on the 22nd December 2022)\n \nPRIVATISATION OF AIRPORTS\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to privatize more airports as part of\nproposed monetisation;\n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n \n(c) the amount of revenue that the Government expects to earn therefrom along\nwith the steps taken to ensure job safety of existing employees serving in the\nairline?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n*****\n*225. PROF SOUGATA RAY\n be pleased to state:-\n (Shri Jyotiraditya M. Scindia)\n\nStatement in reply to parts (a) to (c) of the Lok Sabha Starred (*) Question No. 225\nfor answer on 22.12.2022 regarding \"Privatisation of Airports\"\n \n(a) to (c): As per National Monetization Pipeline (NMP), 25 Airports Authority of\nIndia (AAI) airports namely Bhubaneshwar, Varanasi, Amritsar, Trichy, Indore,\nRaipur, Calicut, Coimbatore, Nagpur, Patna, Madurai, Surat, Ranchi, Jodhpur,\nChennai, Vijayawada, Vadodara, Bhopal, Tirupati, Hubli, Imphal, Agartala,\nUdaipur, Dehradun and Rajahmundry have been earmarked for leasing over the\nyears 2022 to 2025, considering proceeds of Rs. 10782 crore. However, the exact\nvalue of proceeds that the Government would receive is dependent upon many\nfactors including transaction timing, market conditions, investor appetite,\ntransaction terms etc.\n \nInterests of the AAI employees deployed at the airports brought under PPP have\nbeen fully protected. As per the Concession Agreement with the concessionaires of\nrecently leased six AAI airports under PPP, the employees up to the level of\nAssistant General Manager will continue to be posted at respective Airport  for 3\nyears (i.e. 1 year Joint Management period followed by 2 years deemed deputation\nperiod). Also, the Concessionaire is liable to extend the offer of appointment to\nminimum 60% of employees on terms and conditions not inferior to the existing\nterms. Subsequently, employees have the option to join the Concessionaire or to\nreturn to AAI.\n \nThere is however no impact of leasing of airports on the job safety of existing\nemployees serving in airlines.\n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_226": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n       \nLOK SABHA \n   STARRED QUESTION NO.226  \n   ANSWERED ON 22ND DECEMBER, 2022 \n  \nMAINTENANCE OF NATIONAL HIGHWAYS \n†*226.SHRI VINOD L. CHAVDA: \n SHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \n  \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has conducted any survey or study \nregarding sharp turns, potholes, steep grades, narrow/single lanes or \nother accident prone points on National Highways (NHs) in Bhuj, \nAbdasa, Gandhidham, Rapar, Mandvi and Anjar districts of Kutch Lok \nSabha Constituency and in Madhya Pradesh including Panaa, Katni \nand Chhatarpur districts; \n(b)if so, the details thereof; \n(c)whether the Government has initiated/proposes to initiate any \ncorrective measures to make these NHs safe for commuters; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) to (d)  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n  \n  \n\n STATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 226 ANSWERED ON  \n22.12.2022 ASKED BY SHRI VINOD L. CHAVDA & SHRI VISHNU DATT \nSHARMA REGARDING “MAINTENANCE OF NATIONAL HIGHWAYS” \n(a)&(b) Design, construction and maintenance of National Highways \n(NHs) are carried ou t as per Indian Roads Congress (IRC) \nstandards/guidelines, guidelines issued by Ministry of Road \nTransport & Highways (MoRTH), relevant international standards \nand good industry practices . Road safety audit is conducted at \nvarious stages of project impleme ntation like project preparation, \nconstruction and operation following such relevant \nstandards/guidelines. During road safety audit, deficiencies in the \ngeometrics and other features of a road including sharp turns, steep \ngrades, and accident prone points impacting safety of road users \nare identified and necessary corrective measures are taken. \nMinistry and its executing agencies follow standard bidding \ndocuments such as (i) Engineering Procurement Contract (EPC) (ii) \nHybrid Annuity Mode Concession Agreemen t and (iii) \nBOT(Toll/Annuity) Concession Agreement. Such \ncontract/concession agreements have provisions to make the \ncontractor/concessionaire responsible for safety auditing at design \nstage, during construction, before opening to traffic and during \noperations and taking necessary corrective measures which are \nbeing followed in all NH projects. Details of road safety audits \nconducted  in Bhuj, Abdasa, Gandhidham, Rapar, Mandvi and Anjar \ntalukas of Kutch Lok Sabha Constituency  in Gujarat and Panna, \nKatni & Chhatarpur districts in Madhya Pradesh are at Annexure -I. \n \n(c)&(d) Corrective measures from safety requirements are taken as \npart of widening/upgradation projects or on standalone basis \ndepending upon site conditions. Details of the widening/upgradation \nworks and standalone basis road safety works being \nundertaken/completed in Bhuj, Abdasa, Gandhidham, Rapar, Mandvi \nand Anjar talukas of Kutch Lok Sabha Constituency  in Gujarat and \nPanaa, Katni and Chhatarpur districts in Madhya Pradesh are at \nAnnexure-II. Besides, in order to make the NHs pothole free, regular \nrepair and maintenance activities are carried out.  \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE I \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN PARTS (a) AND (b)   OF STATEMENT \nREGARDING REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 226 \nANSWERED ON 22.12.2022 ASKED BY SHRI VINOD L. CHAVDA & \nSHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA “MAINTENANCE OF NATIONAL \nHIGHWAYS” \n  \nROAD SAFETY AUDITS CONDUCTED   ON NHs IN BHUJ, ABDASA, \nGANDHIDHAM, RAPAR, MA NDVI AND ANJAR TALUKAS OF KUTCH \nLOK SABHA CONSTITUENCY \nSl \nNo. \nLok Sabha \nConstituency \nNH No. Length (Km) Road Safety Audit \nConducted in \nLength (km) \n1   \nKutch \nConstituency \n341 162.70 97.5 \n2 754K 264.00 80.00