    "ls|LS17_S10_U_98": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *98 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 13TH DECEMBER, 2022/ AGRAHAYANA 22, 1944 \n(SAKA) \n \nCOLLECTION OF CENSUS DATA \n \n*98.      SHRI A. GANESHAMURTHI: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken any  initiatives for collection of \ncensus data for this decade census and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether any changes in the format or  proforma have been suggested \nfor collection of  additional information for various socio -economic \nparameters and preparation of detailed category -wise database and if so, \nthe details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to include  digital census and self -\nenumeration of citizens, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether there is a demand for conducting caste-wise census also along \nwith the data; and \n \n(e) if so, whether the Government has taken any action in this regard and if \nnot, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n \n(a) to (e):    A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n-2- \nL.S.S.Q.NO.*98 FOR 13.12.2022 \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *98 FOR  \n13.12.2022 REGARDING “COLLECTION OF CENSUS DATA” \n \n(a):  The intent of the Government for conducting Census 2021 was \nnotified in Gazette of India on 28th March, 2019. However, due to outbreak \nof COVID-19 pandemic, the conduct of Census 2021 and the related field \nactivities have been postponed until further orders. \n \n(b):  In Census, data is collected on demographic and various socio -\neconomic parameters like education, SC/ST, religion, language, marriage, \nfertility, disability, occupation and migration of the individuals. The \nquestionnaire for the first phase of Census was notified in the Gazette of \nIndia. \n \n(c):  The forthcoming Census is to be the first digital Census and there is \na provision for self -enumeration. Mobile App for collection of data and a \nCensus Portal for management and monitoring of various Census related \nactivities have been developed. \n \n(d) & (e):  Three State Governments, namely, Bihar, Maharashtra and \nOdisha and a few organisations have requested to collect caste details in \nthe forthcoming C ensus.  In Census, the castes and tribes which are \nspecifically notified as Scheduled Castes (SCs) and Scheduled Tribes (STs) \nas per the Constitution (Scheduled  Castes) Order, 1950 and the \nConstitution (Scheduled Tribes) Order, 1950, as amended from time t o \ntime, are enumerated.  The Government of India has not enumerated caste \nwise population other than SCs and STs in Census since independence. \n******* ",
    "ls|LS17_S10_U_99": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 99 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n  \nNATIONAL STATISTICAL BUSINESS REGISTER \n  \n99.       SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR SINGH: \n                 \n  \n          Will the Minister of STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME \nIMPLEMENTATION be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the ministry has released the results of the 7th Economic \nCensus; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and if not, reasons therefor; \n(c)  the steps being taken by the ministry to  create a National \nStatistical Business Register; \n(d)  the reasons for the delay in creating this Register; \n(e)  whether some States have not approved the provisional results of \nthe census so far due to data quality issues; and \n(f) if so, the steps being taken by the ministry to address this lacuna? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY \nOF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION ; MINISTER OF \nSTATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF PLANNING AND \nMINISTER OF STATEIN THE MINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFIARS (RAO \nINDERJIT SINGH) \n  \n(a) & (b):   No Sir. The ministry has not yet released the results of 7th \nEconomic Census (EC). The provisional results of 7th EC were shared \nwith all State/UTs for their examination and consideration for approval \nby State level Coordination Committee (SLCC).  \n\n(c) & (d):    Development of National Statistical Business Register is a \nfollow-up activity of 7th Economic Census. \n  \n(e) & (f): The data quality issues highlighted by State/UTs \ngovernments are under examination and resolution by the implementing \nagency (CSC SPV) of the 7th Economic Census. The ministry is \nmonitoring the data rectification activities being undertaken by CSC in \ncoordination and consultation with concerned State/UT government. Till \ndate, 6 State/UTs have communicated their approval on the provisional \nresults of 7th Economic Census. \n  \n  \n*** \n "
  }
